{"blocks":[["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-2832","Runs every time a client attaches to the container.",["Hook Families","During normal runtime","DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-2890","Best for interactive or developer-experience tasks that depend on an editor/session attaching.",["Hook Families","During normal runtime","DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-2991","Mechanism",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3007","On first creation, the lifecycle is roughly:",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3275","On a container restart, the creation-time hooks do not rerun:",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3425","On a window reload or reattach, only the attach-time hook runs:",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3538","Practical Distinctions",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3567","DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand vs DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3656","Both are first-creation hooks, but DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand is usually the better fit for project setup because it runs after the workspace is mounted and fully available.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions","DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand vs DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3848","DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand vs DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-3938","DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand is about the container becoming live.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions","DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand vs DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4020","DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand is about a human-facing tool session attaching to that live container.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions","DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand vs DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4136","DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand vs everything else",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4203","DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand is the only standard lifecycle hook in this group that runs on the host rather than inside the container.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Practical Distinctions","DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand vs everything else"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4354","Mental Model",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4373","A useful way to think about the hooks is:",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4419","DevContainer/Hook/initializeCommand: prepare the inputs",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","A useful way to think about the hooks is:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4484","DevContainer/Hook/onCreateCommand: bootstrap the environment once",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","A useful way to think about the hooks is:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4559","DevContainer/Hook/updateContentCommand: reconcile creation with changing workspace content",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","A useful way to think about the hooks is:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4659","DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand: finish project setup",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","A useful way to think about the hooks is:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4726","DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand: re-establish runtime state",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","A useful way to think about the hooks is:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4798","DevContainer/Hook/postAttachCommand: re-establish developer session state",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","A useful way to think about the hooks is:"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4881","Misconceptions",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview"]],["DevContainer/Hook/","source-block-4902","DevContainer/Hook/postCreateCommand and DevContainer/Hook/postStartCommand are interchangeable -> False. One is first-creation setup; the other is every-start behavior.",["DevContainer Hooks Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]]],"format_version":5}